Chapter: RsaDegenerateTest
  cites Foreword chapter Rsa
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 The 2048-bit key, message and OpenSSL signature are codex/test/rsa-verify's. The 512-bit and 1024-bit keys and
 their SHA-256 signatures over "sample" (PKCS#1 v1.5 and PSS with a 32-byte salt) were made and self-verified by
 .NET RSA on Windows CNG, 2026-10-07; the verifier must refuse them by modulus size, and before that floor they verify.

